    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_97a35284",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: stop_racism_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a monkey with the text 'stop racism' and a baby with 'black children and white children are the same,' using the visual of a monkey to imply that Black children are inferior or less human. This is a harmful and hateful stereotype that equates Black people with primates, which is a well-documented anti-Black racist trope. The intent is to trivialize racism by suggesting that racial differences are irrelevant or that Black people are 'the same' as white people in a degrading, animalistic way, thereby undermining the seriousness of racial injustice and perpetuating harmful racial stereotypes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_47bb6560"
      },
